title: The Strike of Capital
subtitle: Industry and the generals move against the workers' government.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1923 and month = 8 and e22_workers_gov > 0 and e23_labour_crisis_done = 0 and crisis = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 3
on-arrival: {!
RG.news('Seeckt demands emergency powers from Ebert', 3);
Q.e23_labour_crisis_done = 1;
Q.inflation = Math.min(100, Q.inflation + 5);
Q.stability -= 6;
!}

= The Strike of Capital

The dollar costs four million marks and the workers' government can no longer pay for the Ruhr. The Reich Association of Industry announces that its members will deliver nothing more to the state on credit, and Hugo Stinnes says in the Reichstag lobby that the currency will be saved the day the government goes. Bavaria stops forwarding its taxes to Berlin.

On 12 August General von Seeckt calls on President Ebert. The army, he says, can no longer answer for order unless the President dismisses the cabinet and gives the emergency powers to him. [? if e22_workers_gov = 2 : Our ministers wait in the cabinet room for Ebert's answer like everyone else. ?][? if e22_workers_gov = 1 : The Chancellor asks whether our deputies and our hundreds will stand by him. ?]

- @defend: Call out the workers and the hundreds to defend the government.
- @councils: Give the power to the factory councils, in the government's name.
- @let_go: Let the government fall rather than fight the army.

@defend
subtitle: [? if lock_uprising = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] A general strike with the unions and the SPD, and rifles behind it.
choose-if: lock_uprising < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids taking up arms.
on-arrival: {!
if (!RG.e22) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.e22_lib.onArrival); }
RG.e22.against('uprising');
RG.ledger('The party called the workers out to defend the workers\' government against Seeckt.', 'e23_defend_wg');
Q.e23_october_path = 3;
Q.crisis_time = 0;
Q.week = 1;
Q.spd_relation += 6;
RG.district('berlin', {guards: 2});
RG.e22.octRise(['berlin', 'saxony', 'halle', 'thuringia'], 'The Defence of the Workers\' Government', 'Hold the districts until Seeckt gives way.', Q.e22_workers_gov == 2 ? 4 : 2);
Q.lean_unionist += 1;
Q.lean_offensive += 1;
!}

The unions, the SPD and our party call a general strike in defence of the government. The hundreds take over the guard of the ministries, and Seeckt orders the Reichswehr to stand by.

@councils
subtitle: [? if lock_councils = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] A rising from below. The SPD ministers are horrified, and Seeckt has his reason.
choose-if: lock_councils < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids it.
on-arrival: {!
if (!RG.e22) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.e22_lib.onArrival); }
RG.e22.against('councils');
Q.e23_october_path = 3;
Q.crisis_time = 0;
Q.week = 1;
Q.spd_relation -= 6;
RG.e22.octRise(['berlin', 'hamburg', 'ruhr', 'halle'], 'The Defence of the Workers\' Government', 'Give the councils the power, and hold it.', 0);
Q.lean_ultraleft += 2;
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
!}

The factory councils of Berlin declare themselves the guardians of the workers' government and take over the food supply.

@let_go
subtitle: Stresemann comes, and the workers ask what we were for.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e22_workers_gov = 0;
Q.e23_cuno_done = 1;
Q.chancellor = 'Gustav Stresemann';
Q.government_name = 'Stresemann cabinet (DVP, Centre, DDP, SPD)';
Q.spd_in_government = 1; Q.zentrum_in_government = 1; Q.ddp_in_government = 1; Q.dvp_in_government = 1;
Q.worker_support -= 6;
Q.stability += 6;
Q.offensive_satisfaction -= 8;
!}

Ebert dismisses the cabinet on 13 August and asks Gustav Stresemann to form a great coalition. Seeckt does not get his powers, yet.
